KZ2 patch 7004: a SPURS task dispatched by the taskset exit scan or by cellSpursCreateTask runs as the task id its
dispatcher chose, passed as an argument (spu_dispatch_async_ids) instead of through the globals
g_ydkj_real_taskset_ea / g_ydkj_real_taskid. cellSpursCreateTask writes those globals outside the scan's lock on its
PPU thread; landing between the scan's write and the dispatcher's read (or spu_taskset_dispatch's), it gave the job
another task's id: the job ran its image with that task's TaskInfo (argument, context), its exit cleared that task's
bits, and its own task stayed enabled and running with nothing behind it. In Killzone 2 (~450 task starts a second in
a level, a third from the exit scan) this stopped The New Sun's load at ~80 s once the per-task log lines no longer
slowed every dispatcher down: Gfx.PB.ShadowMap asserting on a misaligned work pointer (another
task's argument) or the PPU polling forever for a task that never ran. Also: the image-22 (YDKJ cri) paths build
their context from the job's ids; spu_async_run logs "[taskset] MISMATCH" when a job's image is not the ELF of the
task it runs as (always on: a scheduler fault). SPU_TASK_IDS_GLOBAL=1 restores the old hand-over (A/B only).
Host test: tools/spu/test_task_ids.sh. Upstream candidate (the globals hand-over is upstream's; KZ3 patch 1023
moved the writes under the lock but not CreateTask's own store).

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0: context and offsets only.

